// wrangler.template.jsonc is the source and wrangler.jsonc is rendered from
// it by tooling/wire: edit the template, never the render. Two renders:
//
//   - committed: the render from wiring.fixture.json (`pnpm run wire:fixture`),
//     a placeholder project URL and key. `wrangler dev`, the dev verify lane
//     and the composition's structure check (which runs BEFORE the build, in a
//     fresh checkout) all read it, so it has to exist without a build. Edit
//     this file and re-render; tests/web fails when the two disagree.
//   - deployed: the stage and prod lanes re-render it inside their own job
//     tree, before the build, from the wiring document the `supabase`
//     Terraform root lease-publishes (WIRING_SUPABASE_<ENV>,
//     apps/web/component.yaml).
//
// `next build` reads the vars below from whichever render it finds
// (next.config.mjs) and inlines them into the browser bundle, so the browser
// and the Worker always talk to the same project. The workers-assets
// composition deploys one environment per job with no wrangler `--env`, so
// a placeholder token names the environment a render is for.
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "subscription-payments-web",
  "main": ".open-next/worker.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "compatibility_flags": ["nodejs_compat", "global_fetch_strictly_public"],
  "assets": {
    "directory": ".open-next/assets",
    "binding": "ASSETS"
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": true },
  // The Supabase project the Worker talks to, under the template's own env
  // names, and the Worker's own origin (`getURL()`: Stripe's return URLs, the
  // links in auth emails). The anon key is public by design — row-level
  // security protects the data — so it is a var, not a secret. Locally,
  // apps/web/.dev.vars overrides any of them.
  //
  // Not here, by design: SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is a Worker SECRET. It
  // travels in the same wiring document, and the deploy lane pushes it to
  // the Worker with `wrangler secret bulk` (tooling/wire/secrets.mjs) — it
  // never enters a wrangler file or a bundle. The Stripe keys are Worker
  // secrets the owner adds (.dev.vars.example).
  "vars": {
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL": "https://stage-project-ref.supabase.co",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY": "sb_anon_fixture_stage",
    "NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL": "https://subscription-payments-web-stage.your-workers-subdomain.workers.dev"
  }
}
